window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>As the ruler of Magisan, King Ardashir has an important task—to broker a peace deal that will finally end the war. Unfortunately, the price to accomplish it is more than I ever imagined.<br> <br> <i>Me</i>.<br> <br> As his eldest daughter, I, Princess Anna, am sent to the court of the enemy, with only a cold and unflinching soldier named Ravin as my bodyguard.<br> <br> Resigned to my fate, I’m forced to navigate a web of political deception, unsure about who I can trust… including my father. As it turns out, he sent me not only as a token of peace, but as a vessel to secure his victory because Ravin is not my bodyguard, but my father’s secret weapon of destruction. A powerful and ruthless Jinn bound to King Ardashir by dark magic.<br> <br> It’s been a thousand years since I was released from my mystical jinn prison, but with it, came a deadly condition—I was bound to the king of Magisan to be his weapon of war. Once I destroy his enemy’s army, I’ll finally have freedom and nothing is going to stop me… until I lay eyes on his daughter, Princess Anna.<br> <br> With one look at her, I realize she’s the incarnation of my long-lost love, Anahita, a wise water goddess with the power of persuasion. So sure of this, I decide to alter my directive, taking Princess Anna hostage to convince her to help me kill the king, and secure my freedom once and for all so we can be together again.</p>"; 
